# Week 11: roles and owners. Run reset.sql first: 3 rooms, 3 accounts (mina, omar, admin), 5 reservations.
#   mina  -> Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==      (USER)
#   omar  -> Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==      (USER)
#   admin -> Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0      (ADMIN)
# Room changes (POST, PUT, DELETE /api/rooms) now use admin (rule D). Bookings use mina; the owner is the login (rule C).
# Week 10 requests that changed are marked "Week 11".

### 1. List all rooms (expect 200, 3 rooms)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms

### 2. Filter by capacity (expect 2 rooms)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms?minCapacity=6

### 3. Filter by keyword (expect 1 room)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms?keyword=pod

### 4. Both filters (expect 1 room)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms?minCapacity=6&keyword=roof

### 5. One room (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/2

### 6. Missing room (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/99

### 7. Create (expect 201 + Location: /api/rooms/4)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Rooftop", "capacity": 12 }

### 8. Replace (expect 200)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/4
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Roof", "capacity": 10 }

### 9. Replace missing room (expect 404)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/99
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ghost", "capacity": 5 }

### 10. Delete (expect 204)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/4
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0

### 11. Delete again (expect 404)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/4
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0

### ---------- Week 4 additions ----------

### 12. Capacity 0 is rejected by the service (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Closet", "capacity": 0 }

### 13. Capacity 50 is rejected (expect 400)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Seminar A", "capacity": 50 }

### 14. Stats: another controller sees the same data (expect {"rooms": 3})
GET http://localhost:8080/api/stats

### ---------- Week 7: reservations (run reset.sql first) ----------

### 15. Reservations of room 1, ordered by start (expect 200, 3; owners mina, omar, omar)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1/reservations

### 16. Reservations of a missing room (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/99/reservations

### 17. Book room 1 as mina (expect 201 + Location: /api/reservations/6, "owner": "mina")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startTime": "2026-10-14T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-14T11:00:00" }

### 18. Overlaps Mina's 10:00-11:00 on 6 October (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startTime": "2026-10-06T10:30:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T11:30:00" }

### 19. Starts exactly when Mina's ends: touching is not overlapping (expect 201 + /api/reservations/7)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startTime": "2026-10-06T11:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T12:00:00" }

### 20. End before start (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startTime": "2026-10-15T12:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-15T11:00:00" }

### 21. Book a missing room (expect 404)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/99/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startTime": "2026-10-15T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-15T11:00:00" }

### 22. My reservations — mina's, with room names, in one JOIN (expect 200, 4: ids 3, 1, 7, 6). Week 11: was ?reservedBy=Mina
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/mine
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 23. Delete a room that has reservations (expect 409; admin passes rule D, then the 409 rule refuses)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0

### ---------- Assignment 5 ----------

### 24. One reservation (expect 200, owner mina, Seminar A)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/6
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 25. Cancel a reservation (expect 204: mina owns 7)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/7
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### ---------- Week 9 in class: dirty checking and error bodies (rooms) ----------

### 26. Same values again (expect 200; console: one select, no update)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/2
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Study Pod", "capacity": 4 }

### 27. New values (expect 200; console: select, then update)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/2
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Study Pod XL", "capacity": 6 }

### 28. Blank name (expect 400, fieldErrors: name)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "capacity": 5 }

### 29. Capacity 0 (expect 400, fieldErrors: capacity)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Closet", "capacity": 0 }

### 30. Two bad fields (expect 400, two fieldErrors)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "capacity": 50 }

### 31. Missing room (expect 404, message "room 99 not found")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/99

### 32. Room with reservations (expect 409, message "room 1 has reservations")
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0

### 33. A URL that does not exist (expect 404, not 500)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/nothing

### ---------- Week 9 Lab E: reservations and bad input ----------

### 34. Week 11: a reservedBy in the body is ignored. The owner is the login, not omar (expect 201 + /api/reservations/8, "owner": "mina")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reservedBy": "omar", "startTime": "2026-11-02T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-02T11:00:00" }

### 35. Missing endTime (expect 400, fieldErrors: endTime)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startTime": "2026-11-02T10:00:00" }

### 36. End before start (expect 400, message "startTime must be before endTime")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startTime": "2026-11-02T12:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-02T11:00:00" }

### 37. Overlaps Mina (expect 409, message "room 1 is already booked at that time")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/1/reservations
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startTime": "2026-10-06T10:30:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T11:30:00" }

### 38. Missing reservation (expect 404, message "reservation 99 not found")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/99
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 39. Not an id (expect 400, "'id' has the wrong type"). Week 11: the ?reservedBy= search is gone
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/abc
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 40. Not a number (expect 400, "request body is missing or is not valid JSON")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM0
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Lab", "capacity": "ten" }

### 41. Not an id (expect 400, "'id' has the wrong type")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/abc

### ---------- Week 10, hour 2: Spring Security and HTTP Basic ----------

### 42. Create a room without logging in (expect 401, message "login required")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Quiet Room", "capacity": 6 }

### 43. Sign up (expect 201; the body has id, username and role, never the password)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "lee", "password": "lee12345" }

### 44. Same username again (expect 409, "username lee is taken")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "lee", "password": "another123" }

### 45. Bad signup (expect 400, fieldErrors: username and password)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "Lee!", "password": "short" }

### 46. Create a room as lee (Week 11: expect 403, "admin role required" — rule D)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic bGVlOmxlZTEyMzQ1

{ "name": "Quiet Room", "capacity": 6 }

### 47. Wrong password (expect 401, "wrong username or password")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic bGVlOndyb25ncGFzcw==

{ "name": "Quiet Room 2", "capacity": 6 }

### 48. Reading is still public (expect 200, 3 rooms: 46 was refused in Week 11)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms

### 49. Who am I? (expect 200, username lee, authorities include "ROLE_USER")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic bGVlOmxlZTEyMzQ1

### ---------- Week 10, hour 3: a token instead of the password ----------

### 50. Log in (expect 200, accessToken, tokenType "Bearer", expiresIn 1800). The script keeps the token.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "lee", "password": "lee12345" }

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 51. Log in with a wrong password (expect 401, "wrong username or password")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "lee", "password": "wrongpass" }

### 52. Who am I, with the token? (Week 11: expect 200, username lee, authorities include "ROLE_USER")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 53. Create a room with the token (Week 11: expect 403, "admin role required" — lee is a USER)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "name": "Token Room", "capacity": 3 }

### 54. A broken token (expect 401, "token is invalid or expired")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi

{ "name": "Fake Room", "capacity": 3 }

### 55. A broken token on a public GET (expect 401: a token that is sent is always checked)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi

### ---------- Week 10 Lab F ----------

### 56. My reservations without logging in (expect 401, "login required")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/mine


### ---------- Week 11, hour 1: roles (rule D) ----------

### 57. Sign up and ask for ADMIN (expect 201, "role": "USER": the client cannot choose its role)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "kim", "password": "kim12345", "role": "ADMIN" }

### 58. Log in as admin (expect 200). The script keeps the token as adminToken.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "admin1234" }

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 59. Who am I, with the admin token? (expect 200, authorities include "ROLE_ADMIN")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 60. Admin creates a room with the token (expect 201 + Location: /api/rooms/5)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "name": "Admin Room", "capacity": 6 }

### 61. mina creates a room (expect 403, "admin role required")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

{ "name": "Mina Room", "capacity": 4 }

### 62. lee changes room 5 with his token (expect 403, "admin role required")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/5
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "name": "Lee Room", "capacity": 4 }

### 63. Nobody logged in deletes room 5 (expect 401, not 403: we don't know who you are yet)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/5

### 64. mina books room 5 (expect 201 + /api/reservations/9: "/api/rooms/*" does not match /api/rooms/5/reservations)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/5/reservations
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

{ "startTime": "2026-11-20T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-20T11:00:00" }

### 65. Admin deletes room 5 (expect 409, "room 5 has reservations": rule D lets admin in, the 409 rule still applies)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ---------- Week 11, hour 2: owners (rule C) ----------

### 66. mina's reservations (expect 200, 5: ids 3, 1, 6, 8, 9)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/mine
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

### 67. omar's reservations (expect 200, 3: ids 2, 4, 5)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/mine
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==

### 68. omar reads mina's reservation (expect 403, "reservation 9 belongs to another user")
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==

### 69. Admin reads it (expect 200: the owner or an admin)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 70. omar cancels mina's reservation (expect 403)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==

### 71. omar reads a reservation that does not exist (expect 404: we look it up before we check the owner)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/99
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==

### ---------- Week 11 Lab G: PUT /api/reservations/{id} — the owner only ----------

### 72. mina moves her reservation (expect 200, 14:00 to 15:00)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/9
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

{ "startTime": "2026-11-20T14:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-20T15:00:00" }

### 73. The same time again (expect 200: a reservation does not overlap itself)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/9
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

{ "startTime": "2026-11-20T14:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-20T15:00:00" }

### 74. omar moves mina's reservation (expect 403)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/9
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic b21hcjpvbWFyMTIzNA==

{ "startTime": "2026-11-20T16:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-20T17:00:00" }

### 75. Admin moves it (expect 403: changing is for the owner only, not the admin)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/9
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "startTime": "2026-11-20T16:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-20T17:00:00" }

### 76. mina moves reservation 6 onto her own 10:00-11:00 on 6 October (expect 409, "room 1 is already booked at that time")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/6
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

{ "startTime": "2026-10-06T10:30:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T11:30:00" }

### 77. End before start (expect 400, "startTime must be before endTime")
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/9
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

{ "startTime": "2026-11-20T15:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-20T14:00:00" }

### 78. A reservation that does not exist (expect 404)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/99
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic bWluYTptaW5hMTIzNA==

{ "startTime": "2026-11-20T14:00:00", "endTime": "2026-11-20T15:00:00" }

### 79. Admin cancels mina's reservation (expect 204: the owner or an admin)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/reservations/9
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 80. Now room 5 is empty: admin deletes it (expect 204)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/rooms/5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ---------- Week 11, hour 3: CORS (what a browser asks first) ----------

### 81. Preflight from Live Server (expect 200 and Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:5500)
OPTIONS http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Origin: http://localhost:5500
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization, content-type

### 82. Preflight from a page we did not list (expect 403, body "Invalid CORS request" — not ApiError: the CORS filter answers first)
OPTIONS http://localhost:8080/api/rooms
Origin: http://evil.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST

### ---------- Optional challenge: refresh token and logout (not part of 1-82) ----------

### 83. Log in as lee and keep the refresh token (expect 200, accessToken and refreshToken)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "lee", "password": "lee12345" }

> {%
  client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 84. Exchange the refresh token for a new access token (expect 200)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

### 85. Log out (expect 204)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }
